  "title": "b12x dense GEMM: fence stage reuse on every mainloop path",
  "user": {
    "login": "original-el8",
    "id": 1637905,
    "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzc5MDU=",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1637905?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/original-el8",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/original-el8",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/original-el8/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/original-el8/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/original-el8/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/original-el8/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/original-el8/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/original-el8/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/original-el8/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/original-el8/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/original-el8/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "The mainloop producer issued fence_view_async_shared() before a TMA refill of a reclaimed smem stage only on the a16 path. Non-a16 plans selected for GLM-5.3 Flash\u2019s KDA projections (blockscaled, activation_mode auto) also let consumers read the stage through the generic proxy, so without the fence a TMA refill can overwrite a stage that is still being read. Under SM contention, whole 64x128 output tiles come out wrong but finite.\r\n\r\nFound while chasing a rare GLM TP4 device error 6 (NaN logits, first seen in KDA layer outputs from finite inputs) on DGX Spark. Replaying the KDA input/output projections (4096->6288, 2048->4096, TP4 rank 0 weights) in a CUDA graph with fixed inputs while a noise kernel occupies random SMs:\r\n\r\nbefore: 3,050 of 100,000 replays differ from the first replay (GEMMs alone); 287 of 9,561 replays bad for the full KDA layer chain\r\nwith this fence: 0 of 7,222 replays bad for the full KDA layer chain\r\nquiet baseline: 0 mismatches in either case\r\n\r\nMaking every thread participate in the release, without the fence, still failed (2,029 of 100,000).\r\n\r\nValidation: SM121 (GB10) only.\r\n\r\nRe-validated with properly rebuilt kernels: b12x compiles in worker processes, and an earlier \u201cpatched\u201d run had been using unpatched kernels. In the SASS, the fenced builds have 5 FENCE.VIEW.ASYNC.S against 3 in the original. Only mode='quantized' plans are affected (dense MXFP8, 64\u00d7128 or 64\u00d764, TMA, persistent); a16 plans already had the fence.\r\n\r\nGLM-5.3 Flash decode at M=96 on GB10, replay-vs-first-replay under an SM-noise kernel:\r\n\r\nKDA input_proj + o_proj: 2,911\u20133,050 bad per 100k before, 0/100k fenced (3 caches); churn + compaction 0/100k\r\nMLA L43 qkv_a_proj + o_proj + shared expert: 3,431/100k before, 0/100k fenced\r\nfull KDA layer 44: 287/9,561 before (all traced to these GEMMs), 0/43,264 fenced under noise, 0/64,826 baseline\r\nM=16 (all a16 plans): 0 before and after\r\n\r\nSame-tactic timing at M=96: input_proj 113.6 \u00b5s before, 110.1\u2013114.8 \u00b5s fenced; o_proj 21.3 \u2192 22.4 \u00b5s (+5%).\r\n\r\nThe corrupted 16\u00d764 fragments match the last 32-wide K block of one K tile being replaced, i.e. a consumer warp reading a stage after TMA refilled it.",
